WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.790
Heat calcium carbonate strongly,

2
00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:05.270
and it breaks down into calcium oxide.

3
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:07.290
Now suppose you are perfect.

4
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:11.030
You collect every last gram of
calcium oxide the reaction could

5
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:14.830
possibly give: a one
hundred per cent yield.

6
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:18.010
Yet forty-four per cent of the
mass you started with has still

7
00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:21.350
gone, lost as carbon dioxide gas.

8
00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:25.590
So how can a reaction be perfect
and wasteful at the same time?

9
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.650
In this mission, you'll
calculate a percentage yield,

10
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:31.470
and find out why real
yields fall short.

11
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:33.130
You'll meet atom economy,

12
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:36.950
and see why chemists want reactions
that waste as few atoms as

13
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.070
possible.

14
00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:42.910
Your mission: explain how a perfect
yield can still waste atoms.
